& [Purpose]
  + compile one exact supplied RIS-P0 Revision 0.2 envelope into a deterministic effectless materialization work plan and independently verify the complete result
  + make every future material operation dependency denied capability unresolved reason and receipt-candidate boundary inspectable without executing or authorizing any operation

& [ProfilesAndBounds]
  + [RMP-001] request profile is cantor-runtime-closure-materialization-plan-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-runtime-closure-materialization-plan-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-runtime-closure-materialization-plan-verification/0.1 and evidence profile is cantor-runtime-closure-materialization-plan-evidence/0.1
  + [RMP-002] strict compact UTF-8 canonical JSON denies unknown duplicate noncanonical and trailing content and is bounded to outer bytes 2097152 upstream envelope bytes 1048576 evidence bytes 8388608 depth 48 fields 32768 and ordinary text 4096
  + [RMP-003] evidence references are 1 through 64 operation dependencies are 0 through 256 and all byte count ordinal formula and collection arithmetic is checked
  + [RMP-004] input class is exactly synthetic_provider_free_fixture or supplied_unobserved_declaration and the known P0 synthetic request cannot be relabeled as supplied unobserved

& [ExactUpstreamReplay]
  + [RMP-005] request binds distinct nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing request and materialization identities exact upstream canonical envelope bytes byte SHA256 P0 request plan envelope and expected-receipt digests evidence references nonauthority and self-excluding request digest
  + [RMP-006] upstream parser must accept only exact P0 Revision 0.2 canonical UUID signature profiles lifecycle supplied-data authority two roots complete plan expected receipt twenty-five denials and all-zero observation and state assertions
  + [RMP-007] upstream envelope is recompiled from its request and byte-compared before planning; raw-byte stale digest reordered plan denial removal receipt assertion and fully redigested semantic mutation refuse
  + [RMP-008] hashes establish correspondence only and prove no byte presence provenance license policy trust compatibility safety suitability availability acquisition build installation activation or receipt truth

& [ClosedOperationSurface]
  + [RMP-009] phases are exactly seed_validation prerequisite_resolution material_production target_preparation material_staging material_verification rollback_preparation closure_verification and receipt_candidate
  + [RMP-010] operation kinds are exactly validate_seed_root resolve_prerequisite apply_deterministic_transform run_source_build acquire_content_addressed_artifact accept_explicitly_supplied_material generate_configuration prepare_target stage_material verify_material prepare_rollback verify_closure and emit_receipt_candidate
  + [RMP-011] each operation binds ordinal phase kind subject identity exact optional P0 node prerequisite edge and source references dependencies target expected digest expected bytes verifier executable disposition required-but-denied capabilities unresolved reason disposition and self-excluding operation digest
  + [RMP-012] every operation disposition is proposed_awaiting_separate_commission, execution_authorized is false, observed and executed are false and its required capabilities remain members of the conserved denial set
  + [RMP-013] two seed-root validation operations bind exactly the P0 bootstrap and installation-SOP roots in lexicographic identity order
  + [RMP-014] one prerequisite-resolution operation binds every P0 unresolved prerequisite in canonical identity order without reading a host environment network reservoir or secret
  + [RMP-015] each nonroot material has exactly one production operation selected by its unchanged kind and source: derived deterministic transform, built source build, acquired content-addressed artifact, explicitly supplied descriptor or generated configuration
  + [RMP-016] every material node has exactly one target preparation one stage and one verification operation preserving its P0 topological order target expected digest bytes verifier and executable disposition; three terminal operations prepare rollback verify closure and emit one receipt candidate

& [OrderingAndDependencies]
  + [RMP-017] operation count is exactly four times material node count plus prerequisite count plus three and therefore 11 through 1155 under imported P0 bounds
  + [RMP-018] production depends on all prerequisite resolutions plus each input root validation or nonroot production; target preparation depends on prerequisite resolutions; stage depends on its target preparation plus root validation or production; verify depends on stage
  + [RMP-019] rollback preparation depends on every material verification, closure verification depends on rollback preparation and receipt candidate depends on closure verification; missing extra self cyclic forward or cross-subject dependencies refuse
  + [RMP-020] compiler derives operation IDs ordering dependencies phase accounts unresolved accounts and counts from exact P0 data rather than trusting caller order or claims; equal semantic inputs compile byte identically

& [PlanReceiptAndAuthority]
  + [RMP-021] accepted compilation emits materialization_plan_compiled_effectless_awaiting_separate_commission with exact upstream identities nine phases ordered operations all operation digests unresolved twenty-five denials receipt candidate request digest and plan digest
  + [RMP-022] receipt candidate binds upstream expected-receipt digest materialization and operation identities but has zero observations executed operations materialized nodes verified nodes filesystem results verifier results installation activation rollback-ready or successor-recognition assertions
  + [RMP-023] exact capability denials remain filesystem_read filesystem_write filesystem_delete environment_read clock_read process_spawn shell_exec compiler_exec package_manager_exec network_contact artifact_download provider_contact model_load inference mcp_contact git_mutation workspace_mutation secret_access permission_change service_activation cleanup rollback remote_access hardware_effect and external_effect
  + [RMP-024] declaration planning executor host profile artifact resolution installation observation acceptance activation successor recognition rollback execution and cleanup remain separate lifecycle and authority stages

& [VerificationAndFailure]
  + [RMP-025] request operation receipt plan envelope and evidence digests are domain-separated deterministic and self-excluding
  + [RMP-026] independent verification reparses retained exact upstream and request bytes, recompiles P0, compiles materialization plan twice and byte-compares envelope plan verification and reconstructed manifest without trusting producer counts order or digests
  + [RMP-027] verification reports exact upstream roots nodes edges prerequisites phases operation kinds operations unresolved denials evidence references receipt-zero fields and sixteen effect counters; every effect counter is zero
  + [RMP-028] unknown duplicate overbound profile input-class identity upstream byte digest graph source target operation phase order dependency denial authority receipt verification raw-byte and fully redigested semantic mutations fail closed with typed faults and no partial output
  + [RMP-029] production exposes supplied-data parsing strict P0 replay hashing normalization serialization planning and verification only and performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model MCP Git workspace secret permission activation rollback remote hardware or external action
  + [RMP-030] first retained fixture is the exact existing small synthetic P0 closure, remains synthetic_provider_free_fixture and contains no observed host material secret provider model remote or externally acquired byte

& [Acceptance]
  + [RMP-A01] source audit constraint delineation data dual threat seven-fold canonical explosion justification solution plan matrix phase lock proof review satisfaction signature manifest and independent formation verifier agree exactly
  + [RMP-A02] safe Rust exports strict bounded forms exact upstream replay deterministic operation DAG domain-separated digests typed faults receipt candidate and independent verifier using existing dependencies only
  + [RMP-A03] focused success permutation formula phase kind dependency path upstream fixture-class raw-byte denial observation receipt and fully redigested semantic-tamper tests plus bounded CLIs retained evidence and separate verifier pass debug and overflow-checked release
  + [RMP-A04] exact locked offline serialized workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format formation runtime recursive evidence attribution publication remote equality and post-push replay pass
  + [RMP-A05] real closure declaration RIS-P1 executor RIS-P2 host and artifact profiles RIS-P3 activation bootstrap distribution dependency vendoring model or provider acquisition license acceptance secrets remote machines FPGA Minecraft and every physical effect remain separately sourced and signed

& [Invalidation]
